  "obligation": "Execute unshared Memory32/Memory64 and custom page sizes through the existing shared memory cell, scalar ABI and dispatch; preserve unsigned indices and exact offset arithmetic, original imported type/page size/maximum and growth/lifecycle state.",
  "representation": "WasmMemory and the existing traced resource retain the validated MemoryType as authority. Page size, index width, page/address caps, limits, size/growth results and import matching derive from it; implicit and explicit default page sizes compare by actual bytes. Structure admission is separate from host allocation representability, preserving valid maximal module definitions. MemoryAddress uses a raw 64-bit constant-pool offset and resource register; checked u64 addition traps before wrapping or rounding, and the existing WasmBits64 scalar representation carries exact effective addresses. No f64 address transport, Memory32-only offset role, identity side map or second executor. Init uses I32 data input/length and destination width; mixed copy uses each memory width and the smaller length width. Active data expressions validate against owning memory width. Shared index-size/grow-failure projection serves both memories and tables. Residual format53 rejects old MemoryAddress operand meanings; validation rejects non-WasmBits64 offset constants.",
  "scope": "Previous 135-file table/host/import/lifecycle ratchet plus all top-level i64 memory declarations and all five pinned custom-page-sizes proposal files: 151 files. Matching frozen baseline/current directive IDs/input hashes and 60-second completed worker deadlines include ordinary Memory32 load/store/grow/bulk callers. No full Test262, Wasm, Node or benchmark run; production JS/Node execution is unchanged.",
